## Workflow (non-negotiable)

1. Check current branch and working tree; stop if unrelated changes exist.
2. Run the baseline gate on untouched code.
3. Starting a new feature on a team? Run `/claim-feature` FIRST — it allocates
   the feature number and owner on the roadmap before anything else exists.
4. One feature branch per feature. <!-- multi-repo: one branch per affected repo -->
5. Create/update `spec.md` → `plan.md` → `tasks.md` and get approval.
6. Implement **one phase only**, then stop and ask the user to run the gate.
7. The gate is `./gate.ps1` (or `./gate.sh`) at the repo root. The **user** runs
   it; it prints `EXIT: <code>` and writes a receipt. **Do not claim success
   until `./gate.ps1 -Verify` (or `./gate.sh --verify`) reports
   `RECEIPT: valid`** — a pasted exit code does not count, and a receipt from
   before your latest edit reports `RECEIPT: stale`.
8. User checks `git diff --stat`; fix only current-phase issues; commit the phase.
9. AI review (`/phase-review`), then human review, then merge. Never merge on AI
   review alone.

## Strict Rules

- Implement one phase only; do not continue without user approval.
- Do not refactor unrelated files or change unrelated features.
- Do not add packages unless approved in the feature's `plan.md` (a hook enforces
  this — see `.claude/settings.json`).
- Do not change architecture unless approved in `plan.md`.

## Source of Truth Priority

1. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/screenshots/`  <!-- per feature; absent when the feature has no design -->
2. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/spec.md`
3. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/plan.md`
4. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/contracts/`
5. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/data-model.md`
6. `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/tasks.md`

On any conflict between artifacts: **stop and report** — never silently choose.
Never invent a UI layout when screenshots exist.

Phase progress goes in `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/status.md` and feature status in
`docs/roadmap/status.md` — never as edits to `tasks.md` or the roadmap
definitions, which are fingerprinted by the gate receipt. Wanting to change
`tasks.md` after implementation means the requirements moved: stop and report.

Source artifacts each own one dimension of authority — roadmap = scope/status,
`docs/business/` guides = behavior, prototype/screenshots = layout. Specs are
**derived** from them; if a source changes after derivation, report the
divergence (`docs/process/source-artifacts.md`).

## Design Source & Screenshots

Usual design source for this project: {{DESIGN_SOURCE}} <!-- HTML prototype at
{{PROTOTYPE_PATH}} / Figma / AI-generated mocks / mostly no design -->

Per feature, whatever the source, the contract is the same
(`docs/process/source-artifacts.md`):

- If `specs/feature/NNN-<name>/screenshots/` exists (captured/exported from the design
  source, sequence-numbered `01-…`, provenance in `notes.md`), it is the **#1
  layout authority** — the implemented UI must follow it exactly.
- AI-generated designs become authority only **after human approval** promotes
  them to `docs/prototypes/`.
- If a feature has no design, the `spec.md` layout section plus the app's design
  system govern; offer a generated mock for non-trivial UI, and never demand
  screenshots that cannot exist.

